  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA Center Indo-Pacific Minilateral Series: Quad Options 01-23</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This workshop brings together scholars, policymakers, military officers, and security experts to discuss the state of maritime security at the meeting of the Indian and Pacific Oceans; specifically, the geographic area of interest is the Bay of Bengal and Southeast Asia. The program has two specific, interrelated aims to review existing institutions/partnerships/efforts for effectiveness and to propose options for gaps in security architecture that remains. The topics to be covered include commercial technological advancements, Mini lateral formations, non-traditional security approaches, mid-level maritime cooperation, and information sharing, among others. The Quad, while not the overarching focus of the event, will be a prominent component of plenary discussions. The event features several plenary sessions, as well as breakout groups designed to help build policy ideas and recommendations. The event has an overt focus on maritime security and related issues (NESA is partnering with RSIS).</narrative>
  </description>
